    "events": 2000,
    "finding": {
      "index_path_dominates": "~99% of ingest time is the k*t_PRF term -- one sealed index token per keyword and per range prefix. This is the Exp. 1 optimisation lead the plan anticipated, and it is stated here because a decision about it belongs against this end-to-end number rather than a microbenchmark table.",
      "signing_is_not_the_bottleneck": "Total cost is flat across every batch size: at B=1 one ML-DSA signature per event is ~1% of ingest, and at B=512 it is ~0%. t_sign/B is therefore negligible and the batching design is validated rather than merely assumed."
    },
